{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.AbsoluteValue.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.a3_precision_needs_leading_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.a3_precision_needs_leading_channel","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L64-L73","doc":"**Capstone — A=3 precision is Δ_λ-gated, not a higher-order refinement.** The bounded higher-order\ntail is below the miss (`bounded_tail_lt_miss`) while the graded baseline dominates\n(`graded_baseline_dominates`); closing the miss by higher orders needs an anomalous coefficient\n(`required_coeff_gt_thirteen`). So the routine higher-cluster-order route is order-separated out —\nprecision improvement requires a new leading-order (h⁴) channel (the Δ_λ closure). scope-(a); no fit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.graded_baseline_dominates","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.graded_baseline_dominates","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L60-L62","doc":"**The graded baseline dominates** (`ρ_grad_G(3)/ρ_strong(3) > 87%`): the exact, derived term is\nalmost the whole ratio, so all the precision error lives in the small subleading cluster. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.required_coeff_gt_thirteen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.required_coeff_gt_thirteen","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L54-L58","doc":"**A higher-order closure would need an anomalous h⁶ coefficient `a₁ > 13`** — 13× the O(1)\nnatural size (`h² ≈ 0.0437`), a fit red-flag (cf. the Q_β `c₃` `1/u³` hypersensitivity). Here\n`a₁ = Δ/(c₃·h²) = 0.17376892/(0.297·0.0437062)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.bounded_tail_lt_miss","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.bounded_tail_lt_miss","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L47-L52","doc":"**The full bounded (`|aₖ| ≤ 2`) higher-order tail closes ≤ 0.7% of the ratio — ≪ the 4.56% miss.**\nThe geometric tail `c₃·2·h²/(1−h²)` at the corpus values (`c₃ = 0.297`, `h² = 0.0437062`) is\n`< 0.0272`, far below the miss `Δ = 0.17376892`. So even summing every bounded higher order cannot\nclose the A=3 miss. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.bounded_order_term_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.bounded_order_term_le","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/A3PrecisionOrderSeparation.lean#L38-L45","doc":"**Bounded coefficient ⇒ bounded higher-order contribution.** A higher-order cluster term\n`a · c · h²` with a coefficient bounded by `|a| ≤ B` contributes at most `B · c · h²` in magnitude\n(for `0 ≤ c`, `0 ≤ h²`). This is the structural fact behind the tail bound: routine (bounded-\ncoefficient) higher orders cannot exceed `B·c·h²` per order. ","signatureChunk":0}]}